description.content:
Stream real-time progress updates for a PDF generation job using Server-Sent Events (SSE).

    This endpoint provides live progress updates as the PDF is being generated, without
    requiring polling. It uses Redis Pub/Sub to receive events from the ARQ worker,
    making it work seamlessly across Kubernetes pods.

    **Usage:**
    ```javascript
    const eventSource = new EventSource('/api/format/pdf-stream/abc-123');
    eventSource.addEventListener('progress', (event) => {
        const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
        console.log(`${data.progress}% - ${data.message}`);
        if (data.is_complete || data.is_error) {
            eventSource.close();
        }
    });
    ```

    The stream automatically closes when:
    - The job completes successfully (is_complete=true)
    - The job fails (is_error=true)
    - The client disconnects

    Returns:
        - 200: SSE stream of progress events
        - 403: Access denied (job belongs to different organization)
        - 404: Job not found

